IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `jcxv-dates`
IMPORT `jcxv-claims`

-- Jurisdiction of Courts (Cross-vesting) Act 1987 (WA) -- worked cases for the questions of a party to a civil
-- proceeding.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Expected values were written by hand
-- from the text before the file was run; none was copied from the encoding's output. All facts are HYPOTHETICAL.
--
-- Sourced from the Western Australian Legislation website, State of Western Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Short names for the facts used below`

`WASC` MEANS `the Supreme Court of Western Australia`
`FCWA` MEANS `the Family Court of Western Australia`
`other SC` MEANS `the Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory`
`FCA` MEANS `the Federal Court of Australia`
`FamCA` MEANS `the Family Court of Australia`
`elsewhere` MEANS `another court or tribunal`

`MORE APPROPRIATE` MEANS `the court finds it more appropriate that the other court decide it`
`INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` MEANS `the court finds it otherwise in the interests of justice that the other court decide it`
`NEITHER` MEANS `the court finds neither`

`para c or e` MEANS `paragraph (c) or (e) of the Commonwealth Act's definition`
`para a b or d` MEANS `paragraph (a), (b) or (d) of the Commonwealth Act's definition`
`para ba` MEANS `paragraph (ba) of the Commonwealth Act's definition`
`no SFM` MEANS `no special federal matter`

`1 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 3 2026
`28 Feb 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 28 2 2026
`15 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 15 3 2026
`29 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 29 3 2026
`30 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 30 3 2026
`31 Mar 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 31 3 2026
`1 Apr 2026` MEANS `the calendar date` 1 4 2026

§ `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding`

#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: a civil proceeding, which this Act's rules on transfer, removal and appeal can reach (s 3)`
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: a criminal proceeding is not a "proceeding" under this Act (s 3(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: this Act does not apply to the jurisdiction that Part 9.6A Division 1 of the Corporations Act 2001 deals with (s 3A, the text's no)`
-- Both: criminal is answered first.
#ASSERT `s 3, s 3A -- does this Act deal with my proceeding` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: a criminal proceeding is not a "proceeding" under this Act (s 3(1), the text's no)`

-- The s 3(2) reading and the State matter definition.
#ASSERT `the Supreme Court, read with s 3(2)` `WASC`
#ASSERT `the Supreme Court, read with s 3(2)` `FCWA`
#ASSERT NOT (`the Supreme Court, read with s 3(2)` `other SC`)
#ASSERT NOT (`the Supreme Court, read with s 3(2)` `FCA`)
#ASSERT `a State matter` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `a State matter` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`a State matter` FALSE FALSE)

§ `s 4 -- can a court outside Western Australia hear my matter`

-- A negligence claim under WA law, heard in the Supreme Court of Victoria.
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Western Australia hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `yes: that Supreme Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your State matter (s 4(3))`
-- A matter removed under s 8 counts as a State matter (s 3(1)(b)).
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Western Australia hear my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `yes: that Supreme Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your State matter (s 4(3))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Western Australia hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a State Family Court of another State` EQUALS `yes: that State Family Court has and may exercise original and appellate jurisdiction in your State matter (s 4(4))`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Western Australia hear my matter` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE `the Federal Court or the Family Court of Australia (a federal court)` EQUALS `s 4 gives it nothing: s 4(3) and (4) vest jurisdiction in the Supreme Courts and State Family Courts of other States and Territories, not in a federal court; the former s 4(1) and (2) are deleted (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Western Australia hear my matter` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `s 4 gives it nothing: your matter is not a State matter (s 3(1)), and this Act does not say more (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Western Australia hear my matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `no: s 4 gives no jurisdiction in criminal matters (s 4(5), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 4 -- can a court outside Western Australia hear my matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE `a Supreme Court of another State or of a Territory` EQUALS `no: this Act does not apply to the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A, the text's no) -- s 4`

§ `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred`

-- s 5(1): WA Supreme Court to the Federal Court, more appropriate.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court (s 5(1))`
-- s 5(1) has no "otherwise in the interests of justice" limb (edge).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `FCA` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `FamCA` `NEITHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 3(2): the Family Court of WA is "the Supreme Court" for s 5(1).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCWA` `FamCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court (s 5(1))`
-- s 6A(3): a federal matter proceeding in the WA Supreme Court; transfer not required, but may.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `FCA` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not required by s 5(1) (s 6A(3), the text's no), but the Supreme Court may transfer it, and it considers that appropriate in the interests of justice`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `FCA` `NEITHER` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(1) does not require it (s 6A(3), the text's no), and the court does not consider transfer appropriate`
-- One s 6A(1) element missing (the related proceeding has its own (c)/(e) matter): ordinary s 5(1).
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer it to the Federal Court or the Family Court (s 5(1))`
-- s 5(2): WA to another Supreme Court, either limb.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `other SC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `other SC` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer it to that other Supreme Court (s 5(2))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `other SC` `NEITHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 5(3): another Supreme Court to WA.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `other SC` `WASC` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: that Supreme Court must transfer it to the Supreme Court of Western Australia (s 5(3))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `other SC` `WASC` `NEITHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 5(3) is excepted from s 3(2): another Supreme Court to the Family Court of WA is not provided by this Act.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `other SC` `FCWA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not provide for that transfer; the cross-vesting Act of the Commonwealth or of another State may (NOTHING-kind)`
-- s 5(4): between the two WA courts, both ways.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `FCWA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer it to the other of the Supreme Court and the Family Court of Western Australia, which then has jurisdiction in every matter in it (s 5(4), s 4(6), (7))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCWA` `WASC` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer it to the other of the Supreme Court and the Family Court of Western Australia, which then has jurisdiction in every matter in it (s 5(4), s 4(6), (7))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCWA` `WASC` `NEITHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 5(5): the Federal Court to the WA Supreme Court.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `WASC` `INTERESTS OF JUSTICE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Federal Court or the Family Court must transfer it to the Supreme Court of Western Australia (s 5(5))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FamCA` `FCWA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Federal Court or the Family Court must transfer it to the Supreme Court of Western Australia (s 5(5))`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `WASC` `NEITHER` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: on the court's view s 5 does not require the transfer (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
-- s 6A(2): a federal matter proceeding in the Federal Court; s 5(5) does not apply, but may.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `WASC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `may: s 5(5) does not apply (s 6A(2)), but the Federal Court or the Family Court may transfer it to the Supreme Court, and it considers that appropriate in the interests of justice`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `WASC` `NEITHER` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(5) does not apply (s 6A(2), the text's no), and the court does not consider transfer appropriate`
-- Routes this Act does not provide.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `FamCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not provide for that transfer; the cross-vesting Act of the Commonwealth or of another State may (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `other SC` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not provide for that transfer; the cross-vesting Act of the Commonwealth or of another State may (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `WASC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not provide for that transfer; the cross-vesting Act of the Commonwealth or of another State may (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE FALSE `elsewhere` `WASC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not provide for that transfer; the cross-vesting Act of the Commonwealth or of another State may (NOTHING-kind)`
-- Gates.
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` TRUE FALSE `WASC` `FCA` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 5`
#ASSERT `s 5 -- must my proceeding be transferred` FALSE TRUE `WASC` `other SC` `MORE APPROPRIATE` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 5`

§ `s 5(7) -- must my related proceeding follow`

#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the court must transfer your related proceeding to the same court (s 5(7))`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 5(7) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(7) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- must my related proceeding follow` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 5(7) does not require it (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 5(7) -- must my related proceeding follow` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 5(7)`

§ `s 5(8) -- can I apply for a transfer`

#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am the plaintiff, applicant or claimant` EQUALS `yes: as a party you may apply for the transfer (s 5(8)); the court may also act of its own motion or on an Attorney-General's application`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am the defendant or respondent` EQUALS `yes: as a party you may apply for the transfer (s 5(8)); the court may also act of its own motion or on an Attorney-General's application`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I have intervened in the proceeding` EQUALS `yes: a person who intervenes is a party (s 3(1)), so you may apply for the transfer (s 5(8))`
#ASSERT `s 5(8) -- can I apply for a transfer` `I am not a party and have not intervened` EQUALS `s 5(8) names no application by you: it names a party, the court of its own motion and the Attorneys-General (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 5(9) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court`

#ASSERT `s 5(9) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: your lawyer may practise in the other court in this proceeding as in a federal court exercising federal jurisdiction (s 5(9))`
#ASSERT `s 5(9) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 5(9) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`
#ASSERT `s 5(9) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 5(9) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`
#ASSERT `s 5(9) -- can my lawyer act for me in the new court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 5(9) gives your lawyer no right on these facts (the text's no: its "if" fails); the other court's own rules decide`

§ `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court`

-- Paragraph (a), (b) or (d): to the Federal Court.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `para a b or d` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court -- so much of it as is within the Federal Court's jurisdiction, including its accrued jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1a), (2)(a))`
-- Paragraph (c) or (e), with s 6A(1) not complete: still the Federal Court.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `para c or e` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court -- so much of it as is within the Federal Court's jurisdiction, including its accrued jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1a), (2)(a))`
-- Paragraph (ba): the family courts or the NT Supreme Court.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `para ba` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to whichever of the Family Court of Australia, the Family Court of Western Australia and the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory appears appropriate -- so much of it as is within that court's jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1a), (2)(b))`
-- Paragraph (ba) with all the s 6A facts: s 6A(1)(a) needs (c) or (e), so s 6A does not apply.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `para ba` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to whichever of the Family Court of Australia, the Family Court of Western Australia and the Supreme Court of the Northern Territory appears appropriate -- so much of it as is within that court's jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1a), (2)(b))`
-- An s 6(3) order made.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `para a b or d` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: the Supreme Court has ordered that it decide the proceeding itself (s 6(1)(b), (3); the text's no)`
-- s 6(9): appeal after a s 6(3) order below.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `para a b or d` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 6 does not apply to this appeal in the Court of Appeal, because the court below made an order under s 6(3) (s 6(9), the text's no)`
-- s 6A(3): a federal matter proceeding.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `para c or e` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not required: s 6 does not require the transfer of a federal matter proceeding while the related State matter proceeding is pending in a Western Australian court (s 6A(3), the text's no); the Supreme Court may still transfer it if it considers that appropriate in the interests of justice`
-- Does not arise: no special federal matter; pending in the Federal Court.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `WASC` `no SFM` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 6 does not arise: no special federal matter, or the proceeding is not pending in the Supreme Court (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `FCA` `para a b or d` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 6 does not arise: no special federal matter, or the proceeding is not pending in the Supreme Court (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
-- s 3(2): pending in the Family Court of WA counts.
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` FALSE FALSE `FCWA` `para a b or d` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court must transfer it to the Federal Court -- so much of it as is within the Federal Court's jurisdiction, including its accrued jurisdiction (s 6(1), (1a), (2)(a))`
#ASSERT `s 6 -- must my special federal matter go to a federal court` TRUE FALSE `WASC` `para a b or d` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 6`

§ `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter`

#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order that it decide the proceeding itself (s 6(3)); it must weigh the general rule that special federal matters go to the federal courts, and any Attorney-General's submission (s 6(6))`
-- Only one Attorney-General notified (edge).
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before written notice of the special federal matter has been given to both the Commonwealth and the State Attorney-General (s 6(4)(a), the text's no); the court may adjourn and direct a party to give it (s 6(5))`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before written notice of the special federal matter has been given to both the Commonwealth and the State Attorney-General (s 6(4)(a), the text's no); the court may adjourn and direct a party to give it (s 6(5))`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: not before a reasonable time has passed since the notice for the Attorneys-General to consider making submissions (s 6(4)(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `no: the court is not satisfied that there are special reasons, other than the parties' convenience, for it to decide the proceeding (s 6(3), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 6(3) -- can the Supreme Court keep my special federal matter` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `s 6(3) does not arise: no special federal matter pending in the Supreme Court (the text's no)`

§ `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time`

-- Directed 1 March 2026 with 28 days: the last day is 29 March 2026.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `15 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
-- Given on the last day (edge).
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `29 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
-- Given the day after (edge).
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `30 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `no: the notice was not given within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); until both Attorneys-General have it, the Supreme Court cannot order that it keep the proceeding (s 6(4))`
-- Given the day before the direction: counted as day 0.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `28 Feb 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
-- Given on the day of the direction.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 TRUE `1 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
-- Not given; today is the last day; the day after.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `29 Mar 2026` EQUALS `not yet, but still in time: the time the court directed has not run out (s 6(5)(b))`
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 28 FALSE `1 Mar 2026` `30 Mar 2026` EQUALS `no: the notice was not given within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); until both Attorneys-General have it, the Supreme Court cannot order that it keep the proceeding (s 6(4))`
-- 30 days allowed: 31 March is the last day.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- have I given the notice in time` `1 Mar 2026` 30 TRUE `31 Mar 2026` `1 Apr 2026` EQUALS `yes: you gave the notice within the time the court directed (s 6(5)(b)); s 6(4)(a) is met once both Attorneys-General have it`
-- The regulative rule alone: day 0, the last day, the day after.
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- notice on this day is in time` 28 0
#ASSERT `s 6(5)(b) -- notice on this day is in time` 28 28
#ASSERT NOT (`s 6(5)(b) -- notice on this day is in time` 28 29)

§ `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief`

#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `yes: nothing in s 6 stops the Supreme Court granting urgent interlocutory relief, as it is in the interests of justice (s 6(7))`
#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 6(7) does not save it: the court does not find the relief in the interests of justice (the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 6(7) -- can the Supreme Court still give me urgent interim relief` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 6(7) does not reach it: it speaks only of urgent relief of an interlocutory nature (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 6(8), s 7(8) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred`

#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(8) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order under s 6(3)` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 6 invalidates the decision (s 6(8))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(8) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided it after an order under s 6(3) made without the s 6(4) notice` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 6 invalidates the decision (s 6(8))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(8) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order under s 6(3)` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say: s 6(8) and s 7(8) save only a decision made through inadvertence or, for s 7, after the Court of Appeal went on under s 7(7) (NOTHING-kind)`
-- s 7(7) going on does not help a Supreme Court decision under s 6.
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(8) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Supreme Court decided a special federal matter without an order under s 6(3)` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `this Act does not say: s 6(8) and s 7(8) save only a decision made through inadvertence or, for s 7, after the Court of Appeal went on under s 7(7) (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(8) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Court of Appeal decided an appeal that s 7(5) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 7 invalidates the decision (s 7(8))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(8) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Court of Appeal decided an appeal that s 7(5) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not invalid for that reason: nothing in s 7 invalidates the decision (s 7(8))`
#ASSERT `s 6(8), s 7(8) -- is the decision invalid because it was not transferred` `the Court of Appeal decided an appeal that s 7(5) sends to a Full Court of the Federal Court or the Family Court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say: s 6(8) and s 7(8) save only a decision made through inadvertence or, for s 7, after the Court of Appeal went on under s 7(7) (NOTHING-kind)`

§ `s 7 -- where can my appeal go`

`FC judge` MEANS `a decision of a single judge of the Federal Court`
`FamCA judge` MEANS `a decision of a single judge of the Family Court of Australia`
`WASC judge` MEANS `a decision of a single judge of the Supreme Court of Western Australia`
`FCWA judge` MEANS `a decision of a judge of the Family Court of Western Australia`
`magistrate` MEANS `a decision of a court of summary jurisdiction`
`CoA` MEANS `the Court of Appeal of Western Australia`
`Full FC` MEANS `the Full Court of the Federal Court`
`Full FamCA` MEANS `the Full Court of the Family Court of Australia`
`HCA` MEANS `the High Court, with special leave`
`SC not CoA` MEANS `the Supreme Court of Western Australia, other than the Court of Appeal`

#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `FC judge` `CoA` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an appeal from a single judge of the Federal Court or the Family Court does not lie to the Court of Appeal (s 7(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `FamCA judge` `CoA` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an appeal from a single judge of the Federal Court or the Family Court does not lie to the Court of Appeal (s 7(1), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `FC judge` `Full FamCA` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an appeal does not lie from the Federal Court or the Family Court to the other of them (s 7(2), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `FamCA judge` `Full FC` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: an appeal does not lie from the Federal Court or the Family Court to the other of them (s 7(2), the text's no)`
-- Federal Court single judge to the Full Federal Court: not this Act's concern.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `FC judge` `Full FC` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say where this appeal goes (NOTHING-kind)`
-- s 7(3): a WA single judge, no Schedule Act matter.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `WASC judge` `CoA` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: with no matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal is instituted in the Court of Appeal and only there (s 7(3))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `WASC judge` `Full FC` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: with no matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal must be instituted only in the Court of Appeal (s 7(3), the text's no)`
-- s 7(5): a WA single judge, a Schedule Act matter.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `WASC judge` `Full FC` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal goes only to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(5))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `WASC judge` `Full FamCA` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal goes only to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(5))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `WASC judge` `HCA` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal goes only to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(5))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `WASC judge` `CoA` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: with a matter under a Schedule Act, the appeal must go to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, or with special leave to the High Court (s 7(5), the text's no)`
-- s 7(4): a court of summary jurisdiction where an appeal lies to the Family Court of WA.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `magistrate` `SC not CoA` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: no appeal to the Supreme Court from a court of summary jurisdiction where an appeal lies to the Family Court of Western Australia (s 7(4), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `magistrate` `CoA` FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: no appeal to the Supreme Court from a court of summary jurisdiction where an appeal lies to the Family Court of Western Australia (s 7(4), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `magistrate` `SC not CoA` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say where this appeal goes (NOTHING-kind)`
-- s 7(6): Family Court of WA judge, a Schedule Act matter and another matter.
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `FCWA judge` `CoA` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the appeal may be dealt with as if no matter in it arose under a Schedule Act (s 7(6))`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` FALSE FALSE `FCWA judge` `Full FamCA` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `this Act does not say where this appeal goes (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 7 -- where can my appeal go` TRUE FALSE `WASC judge` `CoA` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 7`

§ `s 7(7) -- must the Court of Appeal send my appeal to a Full Court`

#ASSERT `s 7(7) -- must the Court of Appeal send my appeal to a Full Court` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Court of Appeal must transfer it to the Full Court of the Federal Court or of the Family Court, as the case requires (s 7(7))`
#ASSERT `s 7(7) -- must the Court of Appeal send my appeal to a Full Court` TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: the interests of justice require the Court of Appeal to go on and decide it (s 7(7)); its decision is not invalid under s 7 (s 7(8))`
#ASSERT `s 7(7) -- must the Court of Appeal send my appeal to a Full Court` FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `s 7(7) does not arise (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 7(7) -- must the Court of Appeal send my appeal to a Full Court` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 7(7) does not arise (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

§ `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court`

`lower court` MEANS `a Western Australian court other than the Supreme Court and the Family Court of Western Australia`
`tribunal` MEANS `a tribunal established by or under an Act`
`not lower` MEANS `the Supreme Court or the Family Court of Western Australia, or a court outside Western Australia`

#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `lower court` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order it removed to itself, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 8(1)); this Act then treats it as pending in the Supreme Court (s 8(2)), which may later send it back (s 8(3))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `tribunal` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may order it removed to itself, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 8(1)); this Act then treats it as pending in the Supreme Court (s 8(2)), which may later send it back (s 8(3))`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `lower court` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 8 does not allow removal on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE FALSE `not lower` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 8 does not allow removal on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 8 -- can my proceeding be removed to the Supreme Court` FALSE TRUE `lower court` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 8`

§ `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court`

#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `yes: the Supreme Court may transfer it to that other Western Australian court, on your application as a party or of its own motion (s 10)`
-- Each condition failing in turn.
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `no: s 10 does not allow it on these facts (the text's no: its "where" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 10 -- can my consumer protection case go to a lower court` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `not under this Act: a criminal proceeding (s 3(1)) or the Corporations Act jurisdiction (s 3A) (the text's no) -- s 10`

§ `s 11 and s 12`

#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `the written and unwritten law of the other State or Territory under whose written law your right of action arises (s 11(1)(b)); evidence and procedure as the court considers appropriate, from rules a superior court in Australia or an external Territory applies (s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the law in force in the State or Territory where the court is sitting, including its choice of law rules (s 11(1)(a)); evidence and procedure as the court considers appropriate, from rules a superior court in Australia or an external Territory applies (s 11(1)(c))`
#ASSERT `s 11(1) -- which law will the court apply to my claim` FALSE TRUE EQUALS `s 11(1) does not apply: the court will not be exercising cross-vested jurisdiction (the text's no: its "where" fails); this Act does not say which law applies`

#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- do the steps already taken count in the new court` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the new court deals with the proceeding as if the steps taken in the old court, including its orders, had been taken in the new court, subject to any order of the new court (s 11(3))`
#ASSERT `s 11(3) -- do the steps already taken count in the new court` FALSE EQUALS `s 11(3) does not apply: the proceeding was not transferred or removed (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` TRUE FALSE EQUALS `yes: the new court may make an order about the costs of the proceeding before the transfer or removal (s 12)`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` TRUE TRUE EQUALS `no: those costs have already been dealt with by another court (s 12, the text's no: its "if" fails)`
#ASSERT `s 12 -- can the new court order the costs of the earlier stage` FALSE FALSE EQUALS `s 12 does not apply: the proceeding was not transferred or removed (the text's no: its "where" fails)`

§ `s 13 and s 14`

#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `a decision about transferring or removing my proceeding under this Act` EQUALS `no: no appeal lies from a decision about the transfer or removal of a proceeding under this Act (s 13(a), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `a decision under s 11(1) about which rules of evidence and procedure apply` EQUALS `no: no appeal lies from a decision about which rules of evidence and procedure apply under s 11(1) (s 13(b), the text's no)`
#ASSERT `s 13 -- can I appeal that decision` `some other decision in my proceeding` EQUALS `s 13 does not bar an appeal from it; whether one lies is for other law (NOTHING-kind)`

#ASSERT `s 14(2) -- can I enforce the judgment in Western Australia` `WASC` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the judgment is enforceable in Western Australia as if given entirely in the Supreme Court's own jurisdiction (s 14(2))`
#ASSERT `s 14(2) -- can I enforce the judgment in Western Australia` `FCWA` TRUE EQUALS `yes: the judgment is enforceable in Western Australia as if given entirely in the Supreme Court's own jurisdiction (s 14(2))`
#ASSERT `s 14(2) -- can I enforce the judgment in Western Australia` `WASC` FALSE EQUALS `s 14(2) does not reach it: it covers only a judgment of the Supreme Court (or the Family Court) of Western Australia given in whole or in part in cross-vested jurisdiction (NOTHING-kind)`
#ASSERT `s 14(2) -- can I enforce the judgment in Western Australia` `other SC` TRUE EQUALS `s 14(2) does not reach it: it covers only a judgment of the Supreme Court (or the Family Court) of Western Australia given in whole or in part in cross-vested jurisdiction (NOTHING-kind)`
